    "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn><mstyle scriptlevel=\"0\"><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace></mstyle><mn>600</mn><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>15</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>16</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>240</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>.</mo></math>",
    "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>16</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>240</mn></math>",
    "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>a</mi><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>16</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>240</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>704</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>",
    "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>16</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>240</mn></math>",
    "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math>",
    "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>15</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>16</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>240</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>.</mo></math>"
  ],
  "text": "The polynomial \n𝑝\n(\n𝑥\n)\n can be factored as\n𝑝\n(\n𝑥\n)\n=\n(\n𝑥\n−\n15\n)\n⋅\n𝑞\n(\n𝑥\n)\nwhere \n𝑞\n(\n𝑥\n)\n is a quadratic polynomial. Find \n𝑞\n(\n𝑥\n)\n.\n𝑞\n(\n𝑥\n)\n=\n \nx2+16x+240\n\tCorrect\nExplanation\n\nTo factor \n𝑝\n(\n𝑥\n)\n,\n we need to find its other factors.\n\nBecause \n(\n𝑥\n−\n15\n)\n is a factor of \n𝑝\n(\n𝑥\n)\n,\n we know that \n(\n𝑥\n−\n15\n)\n divides \n𝑝\n(\n𝑥\n)\n with no remainder. So, to begin factoring \n𝑝\n(\n𝑥\n)\n,\n we can divide it by \n(\n𝑥\n−\n15\n)\n using synthetic division:\n\n\t\n𝑥\n3\n\t\n𝑥\n2\n\t\n𝑥\n1\n\t\n𝑥\n0\n\n\n15\n\t\n1\n\t\n1\n\t\n0\n\t\n−\n3600\n\n\t\n↓\n\t\n15\n\t\n240\n\t\n3600\n\n\t\n1\n\t\n16\n\t\n240\n\t\n0\n\nTherefore,\n\n𝑥\n3\n+\n𝑥\n2\n−\n3\n600\n𝑥\n−\n15\n=\n(\n𝑥\n2\n+\n16\n𝑥\n+\n240\n)\n,\n\nwhich means that\n\n𝑥\n3\n+\n𝑥\n2\n−\n3\n600\n=\n(\n𝑥\n−\n15\n)\n(\n𝑥\n2\n+\n16\n𝑥\n+\n240\n)\n.\n\nTo see whether the quadratic polynomial \n𝑥\n2\n+\n16\n𝑥\n+\n240\n can be factored any further, we calculate its discriminant:\n\n𝑏\n2\n−\n4\n𝑎\n𝑐\n=\n16\n2\n−\n4\n(\n1\n)\n(\n240\n)\n=\n−\n704\n<\n0\n\nSo, the quadratic polynomial \n𝑥\n2\n+\n16\n𝑥\n+\n240\n cannot be factored over the real numbers since its discriminant is negative.\n\nTherefore, the full factorization of \n𝑝\n(\n𝑥\n)\n over the real numbers is given by\n\n(\n𝑥\n−\n15\n)\n(\n𝑥\n2\n+\n16\n𝑥\n+\n240\n)\n."
}